<!-- The single source of truth for the version this application reports.

     Before this file existed, "2.0.0" was written by hand in two separate places in
     Owner.razor: once for the version stamped into every share README, and once for the
     version in the verification record. Nothing tied them together and nothing displayed
     either, so a share could claim it was made by one version while the verification
     record beside it claimed another, with no test to catch the drift.

     A tagged CI build overrides this with -p:Version=<tag without the leading v>, so the
     demo page and the AppImage published from one tag report one version. Ordinary builds
     use the value here.

     Bump this in the commit that becomes the release tag, so the tag and the checked-in
     value agree even for anyone building from source without the tag. -->
<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version>3.0.0</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
